  "notes": "Cash-basis audit (trimmed pp1-8 = report pp8-13, 24-25). Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (p4); expenditures printed by object only (Personnel, Operating, Supplies, Payroll taxes and benefits, Capital outlays), so object lines take general government/Operating with review. County treasurer receipts 69,368 (p4) split with the p7 budget-to-actual schedule rows (County treasurer receipts 64,395 + Property tax credit 4,682 + Motor vehicle pro rate 123 + Carline 168 = 69,368), as in FY2024; the Statement of Activities prints the 69,368 as Property taxes. transfers_in is the printed Total column net 100,000 (Electric -> Street; General -> Street 113,720 eliminated in Reclassifications). Fund balances (919,330 -> 607,833) recorded as fund balance; cash beginning not printed and ending cash not printed as a single figure (balance sheet p3 prints cash 577,088, county treasurer cash 2,588 and restricted cash 28,157), so cash fields null. Business-type: proprietary statement (cash basis, p6) Total column; interest income nonoperating; Electric transfers out 100,000; no proprietary cash flow statement. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p3; totals equal Statement of Net Position governmental column 607,833), business-type lines and totals from Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1). Detail: the only supplementary schedule (p7) is an all-funds budget-to-actual, so detail is one line per fund column of the governmental funds (p4) and proprietary funds (p6) statements; the County Treasurer's Fund schedule (p8) is not recorded (its receipts flow into the General Fund county treasurer receipts). Read pages 1-8 of 8"
}
